---
import Marketing from '../layouts/Marketing.astro';
import EngagementContact from '../components/EngagementContact.astro';
import {engagementSteps,responsibilities,reporting} from '../data/engagement';
---
<Marketing title="How we work" description="A non-custodial service mandate: agree the markets, capital, permissions and operating limits, then follow activity through the client dashboard.">
 <section class="service-hero work-hero"><p class="section-kicker">How we work</p><h1>A clear mandate.<br/>A visible operation.</h1><div class="service-lead"><p>Agree the work before it starts. Retain control of your assets and follow the activity through the client dashboard.</p><a class="home-button" href="#contact">Discuss your mandate</a></div></section>
 <section class="work-process" aria-labelledby="process-title"><div class="section-intro"><h2 id="process-title">From first review<br/>to ongoing operation.</h2><p>Each engagement is scoped around<br/>the client and market.</p></div><ol>{engagementSteps.map(step=><li><h3>{step.title}</h3><p>{step.text}</p></li>)}</ol></section>
 <section id="responsibilities" class="responsibility-section" aria-labelledby="responsibility-title"><div class="section-intro"><h2 id="responsibility-title">Who controls what.</h2><p>Non-custodial access.<br/>Defined responsibilities.</p></div><table class="responsibility-table"><caption>Responsibilities within the agreed service mandate</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Area</th><th scope="col">Your team</th><th scope="col">Onchain Bureau</th></tr></thead><tbody>{responsibilities.map(row=><tr><th scope="row">{row.area}</th><td>{row.client}</td><td>{row.bureau}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><p class="operating-note">Exchanges and protocols provide the underlying trading environment. Their availability and behaviour are dependencies considered when defining the mandate.</p></section>
 <section id="review" class="work-review editorial-section" aria-labelledby="review-title"><div class="editorial-intro"><p class="section-kicker">Operation and review</p><h2 id="review-title">Visibility throughout<br/>the engagement.</h2><p>The live client dashboard lets you inspect activity and review liquidity against your agreed SLA. Reporting coverage, communication and review arrangements are defined for the markets in scope.</p></div><dl class="review-capabilities">{reporting.map(item=><div><dt>{item.title}</dt><dd>{item.text}</dd></div>)}</dl></section>
 <section class="work-terms editorial-section" aria-labelledby="terms-title"><div><h2 id="terms-title">Terms built around<br/>the work.</h2></div><div><p>You supply the liquidity capital used for the engagement. Service fees, capital allocation, operating limits and objectives are agreed in the mandate.</p><p>CEX operation uses API-key access. DEX operation uses roles and permissions through Safe or Squads vaults. The setup can be adapted to your requirements while keeping the service non-custodial.</p><p>Permission changes, exceptions and the process for changing or ending the engagement are addressed when defining the terms.</p></div></section>
 <section class="starting-brief" aria-labelledby="starting-title"><h2 id="starting-title">Bring us your market.</h2><div><p>For the first conversation, share:</p><ul><li>Your token and project website</li><li>Existing or planned exchanges, pairs and pools</li><li>Your current liquidity setup and available capital</li><li>What you want to improve, and any timing constraints</li></ul><p>These details give us a starting point for scoping the engagement.</p></div></section>
 <EngagementContact subject="Service mandate enquiry"/>
</Marketing>
